You don't immediate engrave to ID unknown wands?

> I am currently twoweaponing Greyswandir and another silver saber, but
> I have Moj tucked away in my bag of holding and I was also granted
> Ogresmasher from my god (left that upstairs)

Grayswandir + silver saber = best weapon combo possible in the game,
IMHO. Mojo is fun to throw with GoP but I'd personally stick with
Gray.

> I found Ludios, but haven't ventured there because I don't have
> =oconflict.

You don't need conflict to clear out Ludios, especially with the
weaponry you have. Though you may want a better AC and more HP. Just
take out the soldiers one at a time.

> So basically I was thinking of wishing for a magic marker so I could
> scribe some ?oEnchant Weapon, since none of my weapons are enchanted,
> but I'm also wondering if with three artifacts in the game I should
> risk wishing for fire/frost brand, since I can get expert in longsword
> presumably at some point.

I'd definitely go with the marker since you've already id'd charging.
Gray is a better weapon than the 'brands as it does double damage
against everything and doesn't destroy potions etc.

> I also want better armor before I use the couple of ?oEA I have
> stashed away. What's worth it? Guantles of power? CoMR (don't think i
> really need it)? T-shirt (so i could enchant it)?

Clear out Ludios before you wish for any of that, especially a T
shirt, which you should be able to easily poly up from the huge pile
of dead soldier armor you'll generate. Exception being if you insist
on using Mojo right away, in which case Gauntlets of power are
required (for Valkyries; other classes shouldn't try throwing that
weapon).

